{"id": "EUVD-2026-101225", "enisaUuid": "597c84f8-02db-37c5-923f-830f5c136560", "description": "Tinyexr through 3.2.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in ParseEXRMultipartHeaderFromMemory() that allows attackers to read beyond buffers due to a stale remaining-size value. Attackers can supply a crafted multi-part EXR file whose later part headers bypass ReadAttribute() bounds checks, crashing applications or leaking adjacent heap memory into attribute values.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:57:39", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/tinyexr-multipart-header-stale-size-oob-read", "https://github.com/syoyo/tinyexr/blob/6f470c9ab24bf3992bc512ce07e8ecb00d9bf105/tinyexr.h#L10551-L10621", "https://github.com/syoyo/tinyexr/blob/6f470c9ab24bf3992bc512ce07e8ecb00d9bf105/tinyexr.h#L1207-L1266", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tinyexr-through-3.2.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-parseexrmultipartheaderfrommemory"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110597", "GHSA-jf92-wjh7-86g3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e37243b1-fefe-36f2-beac-225f0ff15bf1", "product": {"name": "tinyexr", "vendor": {"name": "syoyo"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "85bf7a29-3223-3e54-ac37-015e0bcbc178", "vendor": {"name": "syoyo"}}], "isExploited": false}